time=2026-10-26T17:24:39.626Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-f40f3a4a attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nThe Render function renders the current briefs and blueprints of a record store as one anchored Markdown document.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function is in package document of the module github.com/livecodelife/provenance.\n- The file imports sort from the standard library.\n- The file imports strconv from the standard library.\n- The file imports strings from the standard library.\n- The file imports github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope, using the function Match.\n- scope.Match takes the file path as its first argument and the pattern as its second, both strings, and returns a bool and an error.\n- Render passes each given path to Match as the file path.\n- Render passes each affected_scope entry to Match as the pattern.\n- The Store's List method takes no arguments and returns a slice of strings holding record ids, sorted, and an error.\n- The Store's Load method takes a record id string and returns a Record pointer, a Document pointer and an error.\n- The Record's EffectiveType method takes no arguments and returns a record Type, and an empty stored type counts as blueprint.\n- Render reads the Record fields Title (string), ID (string), Version (int), Intent (string), Constraints (slice of strings), Implements (string), ImplementsRepo (string), AffectedScope (slice of strings) and Status.\n- The RenderOptions and the escapeLine function, defined in the same package, are used as their own records describe them; escapeLine takes a line string and returns a string.\n- Render takes a record Store and a RenderOptions value as two positional arguments.\n- Render returns the document as a string and an error.\n- Render returns an empty string and the error when listing records fails.\n- Render returns an empty string and the error when loading a record fails.\n- Render includes a record only when its effective type is brief or blueprint.\n- Render leaves out a record whose status is deprecated.\n- Render leaves out a record whose status is superseded.\n- When Scopes is empty, Render applies no scope filter.\n- When Scopes is not empty, Render keeps a record only when at least one entry of its affected_scope matches at least one of the given paths according to Match.\n- When Match returns an error, Render returns an empty string and that error.\n- Render lists briefs first, sorted by id ascending.\n- Render follows each brief with the blueprints whose Implements names that brief, sorted by id ascending.\n- Render counts only blueprints whose ImplementsRepo is empty as implementing a brief in the document.\n- Render lists the remaining blueprints last, sorted by id ascending.\n- Render writes a brief heading as two number signs, a space and the title.\n- Render writes a blueprint heading as three number signs, a space and the title.\n- Render collapses every run of whitespace in a title to a single space before writing the heading.\n- When IDs is true, Render appends a space and the record id in parentheses to the heading text.\n- When IDs is false, the record id appears in the output only inside the anchor line.\n- Directly after the heading line Render writes the anchor line <!-- provenance:ID@VERSION -->, with ID the record id and VERSION the record's current version in decimal digits.\n- The anchor line has exactly one space after the opening and before the closing comment marker.\n- After the anchor line Render writes one blank line.\n- When the intent is empty, Render writes no intent lines.\n- After the intent Render writes one blank line and then the line **Constraints**.\n- Render writes the Constraints line even when the record has no constraints.\n- After the Constraints line Render writes one list item per constraint, in the record's order, with surrounding whitespace removed from the constraint.\n- Render starts the first line of a list item with a hyphen and a space.\n- Render starts each further line of a multi-line constraint with two spaces.\n- Render writes a blank line inside a constraint as two spaces.\n- Render separates sections with one blank line.\n- The document ends with exactly one newline when it holds at least one section.\n- The document is the empty string when it holds no section.\n- Rendering the same store with the same options twice gives byte-identical output.\n- Render never creates, edits or deletes any record.\n- The file imports github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record, using the identifiers Store, Record, Document, Type and Status.\n- After the blank line Render removes the surrounding whitespace of the whole intent text once.\n- Render then splits the trimmed intent text on newlines.\n- Render keeps each line's own leading and trailing whitespace untouched.\n- Render passes each intent line through escapeLine and writes the result, so the line '  ### x' is written as '\\  ### x'.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for growing the document library (package document, directory document/)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/document-context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the records.\n\n- Package document lives in the directory document/ of the module github.com/livecodelife/provenance. Each imprint owns the file named in its scope (render.go, parse.go, plan.go, apply.go).\n- Where a record states a message as \"The message of X is: text.\" the final period ends the sentence; the message is the text without it (for example `a reason is required`).\n- Where a record states a heading, anchor or marker line, write it with the exact characters stated; do not add or drop spaces.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean. Each import is its own addImport, owned by exactly one record per file; every other record in the file adds no imports.\n- Other records of this package export the types Section, Change, Problem, Plan, RenderOptions, Revised, ApplyOptions and the functions Render, Parse, BuildPlan, Apply as their own records state; call them, do not redefine them.\n- The record package is github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record; its Store interface has List() ([]string, error), Load(id string) (*Record, *Document, error), Save(*Record, *Document) error and Versions(id string) ([]int, error); the scope package is github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope with Match(filePath, pattern string) (bool, error).\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"path\":\"sort\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"path\":\"strconv\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func Render(store record.Store, opts RenderOptions) (string, error) {\\n\\tids, err := store.List()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar briefs, blueprints []*record.Record\\n\\tfor _, id := range ids {\\n\\t\\trec, _, err := store.Load(id)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\ttyp := rec.EffectiveType()\\n\\t\\tif typ != record.TypeBrief \\u0026\\u0026 typ != record.TypeBlueprint {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif rec.Status == record.StatusDeprecated || rec.Status == record.StatusSuperseded {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif len(opts.Scopes) \\u003e 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\tkeep := false\\n\\t\\t\\tfor _, pattern := range rec.AffectedScope {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor _, path := range opts.Scopes {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tok, err := scope.Match(path, pattern)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif ok {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tkeep = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif keep {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif !keep {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif typ == record.TypeBrief {\\n\\t\\t\\tbriefs = append(briefs, rec)\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tblueprints = append(blueprints, rec)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tsort.SliceStable(briefs, func(i, j int) bool { return briefs[i].ID \\u003c briefs[j].ID })\\n\\tsort.SliceStable(blueprints, func(i, j int) bool { return blueprints[i].ID \\u003c blueprints[j].ID })\\n\\tattached := make(map[string]bool)\\n\\tvar sections []string\\n\\tfor _, brief := range briefs {\\n\\t\\tsections = append(sections, renderSection(brief, \\\"## \\\", opts.IDs))\\n\\t\\tfor _, bp := range blueprints {\\n\\t\\t\\tif bp.ImplementsRepo == \\\"\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 bp.Implements == brief.ID {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tattached[bp.ID] = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tsections = append(sections, renderSection(bp, \\\"### \\\", opts.IDs))\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, bp := range blueprints {\\n\\t\\tif !attached[bp.ID] {\\n\\t\\t\\tsections = append(sections, renderSection(bp, \\\"### \\\", opts.IDs))\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(sections) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn strings.Join(sections, \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\") + \\\"\\\\n\\\", nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"Render\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func renderSection(rec *record.Record, prefix string, withIDs bool) string {\\n\\ttitle := strings.Join(strings.Fields(rec.Title), \\\" \\\")\\n\\theading := prefix + title\\n\\tif withIDs {\\n\\t\\theading += \\\" (\\\" + rec.ID + \\\")\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\tlines := []string{\\n\\t\\theading,\\n\\t\\t\\\"\\u003c!-- provenance:\\\" + rec.ID + \\\"@\\\" + strconv.Itoa(rec.Version) + \\\" --\\u003e\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\\"\\\",\\n\\t}\\n\\tif intent := strings.TrimSpace(rec.Intent); intent != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(intent, \\\"\\\\n\\\") {\\n\\t\\t\\tlines = append(lines, escapeLine(strings.TrimSpace(line)))\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tlines = append(lines, \\\"\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tlines = append(lines, \\\"**Constraints**\\\")\\n\\tfor _, constraint := range rec.Constraints {\\n\\t\\tparts := strings.Split(strings.TrimSpace(constraint), \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\t\\tfor i, part := range parts {\\n\\t\\t\\tswitch {\\n\\t\\t\\tcase i == 0:\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlines = append(lines, \\\"- \\\"+part)\\n\\t\\t\\tcase part == \\\"\\\":\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlines = append(lines, \\\"  \\\")\\n\\t\\t\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlines = append(lines, \\\"  \\\"+part)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn strings.Join(lines, \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n}\",\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"renderSection\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- document/render.go: addImport {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-400f65dc; do not select)\n- document/render.go: setType {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"Change\"} (owned by prov-2026-2b7b6b93; do not select)\n- document/render.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"isMarkerLine\"} (owned by prov-2026-400f65dc; do not select)\n- document/render.go: setType {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"RenderOptions\"} (owned by prov-2026-477b93e0; do not select)\n- document/render.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"escapeLine\"} (owned by prov-2026-5e341891; do not select)\n- document/render.go: setType {\"file\":\"document/render.go\",\"name\":\"Plan\"} (owned by prov-2026-6eeaa2bc; 